meta {
  name: S28 first routed record (M-X1a)
  seq: 24
}

docs {
  Story S28, TICK-879; kit P9-05 (TICK-884), ADR-008 X1a / M-X1a. A tenant onboarded in this run (not a seeded one): its first admin publishes a type from the handbook example `docs/handbook/examples/incident.json`, publishes a workflow written from the handbook's example (tour step 8), creates an incident and waits for the workflow to route it. The clock starts at S28.2's 201 and stops at the `source: workflow` history entry (S28.13), which logs the total. Needs the stack and `tools/tunnels.sh up` (nava-onboard publishes no port); no `tools/seed.sh`. S28.3 to S28.5 are a **local-stack stand-in for the customer's company login** and use the Keycloak master admin (a platform-staff action): the stack has no customer IdP, so the brokered first login that creates the admin's user is replayed through the admin API. A timed run counts them as `needed help` (finding F1 of `docs/quality/x1a-first-routed-record.md`). S28.7 waits for one group-sync cycle (up to `s28_place_limit_s`, default 360 s; set `NAVA_GROUPSYNC_INTERVAL=15s` for seconds). S28.12 waits up to 300 s after the create for the route (the workflow waits one minute). Runs again on the same stack: every pass onboards a new tenant.
}
